[**Gold Coast @ Fradgley Hall**](https://www.facebook.com/events/231604530365710/ "Bassidi Kone @ Gold Coast")

Saturday 5th July 2.30-4pm Early Bird (May) $25 Presale (June) $28 Door $32

BASSIDI KONÉ a well renowned, versatile percussionist and balafon player of exceptional talent, that gives a skilled, authentic and dynamic voice to his instruments.

 Bassidi is of Bobo origin (tribe), whose family originates in a village near Segou, (Mali, West Africa). Coming from a musical (Griot) family, Bassidi played music from the age of 5, taught to him by his father and grandfather.

 Bassidi has received numerous awards and achievements for balafon and djembe. Bassidi has released two albums with SAMBA LOLO Recording Productions, Boston, USA . He has independently produced his third album, some of which was recorded at Salif Keita’s studio in Bamako. He will be showcasing this album on this tour.  He has worked with other renowned professionals including Grammy Award nominee, Bassekou Kouyaté, Nainy Diabate, Mah Kouyate No 1, Nafi Diabate.

 This phenomenal musician is set to arrive in the Sunshine Coast June 27th with exciting performances and workshops in the Sunshine Coast, Gold Coast, Brisbane and Byron Bay. Bassidi Koné is an incredible performer and a supportive teacher with an infectious smile.

